<title>INDIA: Indian silver rises on world prices, gold eases.</title>
<headline>Indian silver rises on world prices, gold eases.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices rose on Tuesday helped by a recovery in world prices and fresh seasonal local demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>Silver gained 50 rupees per kg to 6,910, following up Monday's rise of 10 after falling 70 last week.</p>
<p>Gold failed to hold early gains on demand resistance and scattered profit-taking, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices of gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) finished steady at 60,100 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>Sentiment at the close was steady and traders expected higher demand ahead of Diwali, or Festival of Lights.  </p>
